WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.520
Commander McGrath, one of the most influential&nbsp;
members of Mobile Task Force Alpha-1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.280
better known as the Red Right Hand,&nbsp;
had been summoned by his masters for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.240
one of the most important missions of&nbsp;
his life. It was so above top secret,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.360
even he would likely need to undergo amnestic&nbsp;
treatment once he’d seen the job through.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.400
It comes with the territory when&nbsp;
you’re dealing with SCP-006.&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.440
The Red Right Hand is no ordinary Mobile&nbsp;
Task Force, either. They were the personal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:35.760
enforcers of the O5 Council, the thirteen&nbsp;
most powerful members of the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.560
and by extension, some of the most&nbsp;
powerful human beings on earth.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.440
Commander McGrath stood&nbsp;
before the assembled Council,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.280
trying to suppress the tremors of&nbsp;
fear and awe running through him.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:53.120
He’d gone toe to toe with SCP-076, Able, one&nbsp;
of the finest humanoid warriors ever known,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:59.600
during one of his many containment breaches.&nbsp;
He’d led strike forces after a fleeing SCP-682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.720
the Hard to Destroy Reptile, after it escaped&nbsp;
its acid tank and began charging towards the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:10.080
nearest populated area intent on causing&nbsp;
mass death. He’d personally taken out more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.840
people than you’ve probably even met, all&nbsp;
at the behest of his Foundation superiors.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:21.520
And yet, standing right here, before them, he&nbsp;
couldn’t help feel a twinge of deep terror.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:25.840
It was like staring right into the face&nbsp;
of God, and waiting for it to blink.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:32.640
With his well-honed military observation skills,&nbsp;
he noted that O5-2 wasn’t among the council this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:39.520
time, but he knew better than to ask why. He was&nbsp;
employed to take orders, not ask questions. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:45.840
this time, his orders were something special:&nbsp;
He wasn’t given any more information than this…

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.120
“McGrath, we need you to lead an&nbsp;
elite team to Astrakhan in Russia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:54.080
on the double. Procedure 006 is now&nbsp;
in effect. You know what to do.”

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.200
McGrath nodded. He’d been prepared for this&nbsp;
day. His predecessor, Commander Richards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:05.680
had only needed to enact Procedure 006 once in his&nbsp;
long and storied career with the Red Right Hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.880
It was truly a once in a lifetime assignment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.560
and now, the torch had been passed to him. The&nbsp;
only question was whether he’d be up to the task,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:20.000
but McGrath didn’t have time to ponder on&nbsp;
this question. Time was of the essence.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.760
First, he needed to assemble a team - small, but&nbsp;
focused. Loyal men who’d keep their heads down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.160
complete the mission, and take the forbidden&nbsp;
knowledge no further than the bounds of said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.400
mission. McGrath selected three&nbsp;
operatives: Bennett, DiMaggio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.680
and Stuart, all of whom had proven valuable&nbsp;
assets in prior missions. They would be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:46.800
ones to accompany him on this most valuable&nbsp;
and secretive of directives: Procedure 006

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.040
But before they could execute the mission&nbsp;
itself, they needed to be trained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.000
briefed, and fitted with the proper equipment.&nbsp;
For a mission this sensitive, and dealing with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:03.600
an anomaly as deadly as SCP-006, they needed&nbsp;
to wear modified Class VI BNC suits. These are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:09.520
the ultimate, total-exclusion hazmat suits,&nbsp;
designed specifically by the SCP Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:15.040
They offered such a degree of protection that&nbsp;
they made regular hazmat suits look like bikinis.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.920
Commander McGrath actually knew&nbsp;
very little about SCP-006 and how it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.240
worked. Like many of the more top-secret&nbsp;
anomalies contained by the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:29.360
only the O5 Council understood the full scope&nbsp;
of it. Everyone below them were only told the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:35.120
specific fragments of information they needed&nbsp;
to do their job. After all, filling your head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:41.600
with the wrong kinds of knowledge can get your&nbsp;
memory wiped, or worse, at the SCP Foundation.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:47.280
SCP-006, as far as Commander McGrath knew,&nbsp;
was the more traditional kind of toxic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:55.520
He’d been briefed using the SCP-006B Infopack,&nbsp;
a heavily redacted description of 006:

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:00.000
Safe Class, liquid in nature, but one&nbsp;
of the most toxic substances known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.480
to man. It made mercury and uranium look like a&nbsp;
glass of mineral water. And more dangerous still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:12.000
if someone came into contact with even&nbsp;
the tiniest quantity of SCP-006’s liquids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.240
they would not only be marked for certain death,&nbsp;
they would also become a vector for transmission.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:23.360
A veritable plague rat. A&nbsp;
walking danger to all mankind.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:29.920
That’s why the Class VI BNC suits needed to be&nbsp;
tested. McGrath, Bennett, DiMaggio, and Stuart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:35.760
suited up in a secure Foundation training facility&nbsp;
and fully submerged themselves in a training pool.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:39.760
This was how they made sure that there&nbsp;
were no vulnerabilities in the suits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:45.040
If any bubbles were generated, it meant&nbsp;
there was a leak. And if there was a leak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:49.760
then the person wearing the defective suit was&nbsp;
as good as dead when they reached the real 006.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:55.840
Lucky for them, no leaks. They were ready&nbsp;
to proceed to the next stage of the mission:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:03.360
Making their way to Astrakhan, Russia, where&nbsp;
SCP-006 was contained. The pressure was on, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:08.720
the council growing more impatient by the moment,&nbsp;
so they needed to make the journey immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:14.000
Every minute counted, and Commander McGrath&nbsp;
was painfully aware of the time slipping away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:19.440
Though he couldn’t possibly fathom why they’d&nbsp;
need a toxic chemical like this with such urgency.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:24.160
They made their journey in a covert cargo plane.&nbsp;
It was beyond important to keep all Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:30.160
activity around SCP-006 under wraps. A number&nbsp;
of Group of Interest cells were active in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:35.440
area - including the Church of the Broken God&nbsp;
and the Serpent’s Hand. And if ever the dreaded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:41.920
Chaos Insurgency caught wind of SCP-006’s&nbsp;
existence and triangulated its location,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:45.440
the damage it could do would&nbsp;
be unprecedented. That’s why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:50.960
nobody but the O5 Council could truly be&nbsp;
trusted with this almost sacred knowledge.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:55.600
When they touched down in Astrakhan, they met with&nbsp;
a Foundation courier who would take them on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:01.600
final leg of their journey to the Foundation&nbsp;
site, roughly 60 kilometers West of the town.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:06.640
McGrath and his team had no idea what they were&nbsp;
heading towards, or the insane history of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:13.680
land they traversed, all because of SCP-006.&nbsp;
The Foundation had first become aware of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:20.160
the anomaly back during the 19th century, but&nbsp;
were unable to gain control of it until 1991,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:25.040
due to it being fiercely guarded by a&nbsp;
procession of territorial Russian rulers.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:29.760
The blood of hundreds of thousands had been&nbsp;
spilled on this land in historic wars and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:37.840
conflicts over SCP-006. So many had wasted their&nbsp;
entire lives unsuccessfully trying to find it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:42.320
During the several hour car trip to the&nbsp;
site, Commander McGrath had no idea of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:47.120
the true value of the anomaly he and&nbsp;
his small team were heading towards.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:52.240
But he would, in time. Though an&nbsp;
innocent would have to die first.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:57.040
The courier dropped the four operatives off&nbsp;
outside an abandoned chemical plant in the styx,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:02.080
far from what anyone would call civilization.&nbsp;
It was the kind of industrial decay you could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:08.080
expect in the badlands of rural Russia, a&nbsp;
huge complex, weathered and broken by time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:12.320
But what the untrained observer wouldn’t&nbsp;
realize is that the plant was actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:17.760
full of heavily-trained, and even more&nbsp;
heavily armed Foundation security personnel.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:20.800
As McGrath’s team approached the&nbsp;
building, they had no less than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:24.960
eight sniper rifles pointed at them from&nbsp;
various vantage points within the plant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:31.360
just to be safe. The Foundation couldn’t&nbsp;
afford to take any chances with SCP-006.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.840
They arrived at the gate and provided their&nbsp;
clearance credentials. They were envoys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:41.280
here on behalf of the O5 Council themselves, and&nbsp;
if they weren’t allowed to complete their mission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:46.240
then the 006 personnel would have the&nbsp;
death of a Council member on their hands.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:51.840
With that, the team was given a free pass into&nbsp;
the site, under close observation. Anyone seeking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:58.880
to interface SCP-006 was forced to do so under&nbsp;
almost microscopic scrutiny. Even when inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:04.320
the building, McGrath and his men needed to pass&nbsp;
multiple secure checkpoints throughout the halls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.600
each time restating their security credentials.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:11.040
Eventually, they reached a different&nbsp;
section of the building. Forbidding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:16.320
anonymous hallways gave way to what seemed&nbsp;
like a mix of a garden and a jungle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:23.280
But the plants were...different. The trees, the&nbsp;
shrubs, even the weeds, were unlike anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:28.720
members of the team had ever seen before.&nbsp;
It was like stepping into an alien world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:36.240
or perhaps this would, but as it was a few million&nbsp;
years prior. It was terrifying and wondrous.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:42.320
They suited up in their Class VI BNC suits,&nbsp;
fearing airborne contaminants from SCP-006,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:47.440
before proceeding further. They walked through&nbsp;
this new jungle, being watched at every turn by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:52.320
security cameras and personnel posted throughout&nbsp;
this overgrown portion of the facility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:59.120
It didn’t take long for them to reach&nbsp;
their destination, the legendary SCP-006:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:05.200
A small natural spring jutting out of a&nbsp;
rock, surrounded by rich, emerald grass.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:10.320
It looked more like a nice place to have a picnic&nbsp;
than a dangerous and highly secretive anomaly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:17.120
but McGrath wasn’t paid to question things, only&nbsp;
to carry out Procedure 006. The only object they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:22.000
had with them was a Quad-Sealant Container,&nbsp;
an ultra-secure liquid containment unit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:28.720
specifically designed for safely transporting&nbsp;
samples of SCP-006’s water between sites.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:33.680
The team members descended into the spring,&nbsp;
and began filling up the container. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:38.320
nerve-wracking, knowing the stakes of their&nbsp;
mission, and knowing that they were submerged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:44.240
in such a deadly substance. But they had&nbsp;
a job to do, and they were going to do it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:48.080
come hell or high water. They&nbsp;
filled the containment unit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:53.600
but sadly for McGrath and his team, this&nbsp;
mission wouldn’t be entirely without casualty.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:56.480
A single bubble rose from&nbsp;
the leg of Stuart’s suit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:01.440
He was a good MTF Operative, but the youngest&nbsp;
and least experienced member of the team.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:05.040
His suit must have been somehow&nbsp;
damaged during transit, and now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.640
he was compromised. He shared a haunted glance&nbsp;
with McGrath and his fellow team members, knowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:16.320
that his part of the mission, and his life,&nbsp;
was about to come to a swift and violent end.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:21.360
Alarms rang out across the facility. A huge&nbsp;
team of armed operatives, all wearing Class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:27.360
VI BNC suits, charged into the room. Stuart was&nbsp;
grabbed and manhandled out of the 006 spring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:31.760
while his fellow team members sealed the&nbsp;
containment unit and continued their mission.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:38.080
There was no time to stop, rest, or mourn.&nbsp;
Completing the mission was the absolute priority.

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:40.960
If McGrath understood the protocol&nbsp;
as well as he thought he did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:46.000
Stuart would be dragged into a secure room by&nbsp;
the site staff, and locked in with a blast door.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:51.520
He would look down and notice the floor below&nbsp;
him was a metal grate, caked with ash. His last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:56.400
thoughts, as the incinerator launches it’s&nbsp;
flames into action, would strangely be that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:00.960
he was feeling the healthiest he’d been in&nbsp;
years. But that wouldn’t stop the sudden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:06.720
furnace around him from decimating his body and&nbsp;
leaving little more than ash and charred bones.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.960
Over a decade of loyal MTF&nbsp;
service, ended in an instant.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:15.360
Stuart would have been terminated. According&nbsp;
to orders from the top, it was all that could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:21.840
be done for those affected by SCP-006. A&nbsp;
mercy, really, if they were to be believed.

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:26.640
McGrath and his team soldiered on. After&nbsp;
retrieving the sample, they were hurried back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:32.160
their inception point: One of the many classified&nbsp;
bases occupied by the O5 Council members.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:36.400
While DiMaggio and Bennett were ushered off&nbsp;
to be given amnestic treatment, McGrath would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:41.520
personally get to see the containment unit and its&nbsp;
precious cargo make the final leg of the journey.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:48.240
He was going to be granted access to O5-2,&nbsp;
the person this had all been in service of.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:51.600
Commander McGrath approached the&nbsp;
secure quarters of the Council member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:54.880
escorted by a bevy of heavily&nbsp;
armed security personnel.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:12:01.200
The doors opened, and he saw her there, O5-2.&nbsp;
Bedridden, laying at the center of a grand web&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:06.640
of life-saving technology. She was beyond&nbsp;
old and decrepit - Commander McGrath could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:12.000
see the centuries she’d endured written deeply&nbsp;
in the wrinkles and scars of her ancient face.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.840
She didn’t look like one of the most powerful&nbsp;
people in the world, she looked like one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:20.560
the most feeble. Her eyes lit up when McGrath&nbsp;
entered the room holding the containment unit.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:24.960
She beckoned him closer, until he was close&nbsp;
enough for her to take the containment unit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:31.440
from him with scarred, trembling hands. McGrath&nbsp;
watched in horror, as she disengaged the lid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:34.320
and swigged down the entirety of its contents.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.880
But wasn’t the water toxic? He thought.

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:42.480
McGrath had been fed the same lie as everybody&nbsp;
else. The Foundation didn’t keep 006 such a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:47.840
well-guarded secret because it was capable of&nbsp;
bringing death. Quite the opposite, in fact.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:54.480
All Commander McGrath could do was stare,&nbsp;
awestruck, as the years seemed to fall from O5-2’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.480 --> 00:13:02.400
face. Decades and decades and decades. Scars&nbsp;
faded. Wrinkles disappeared. Little by little,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:08.640
O5-2 began to sit, and then stand. By the time&nbsp;
she was straightening her clothes, she looked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:14.160
like a healthy woman in her mid-forties.&nbsp;
It was a complete and total transformation.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:20.160
The liquid of SCP-006 has a plethora of benefits&nbsp;
to human subjects: the ability to regenerate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:26.000
damaged DNA, by heightened excitement of cellular&nbsp;
duplication, and producing a frightening increase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:31.760
in the effectiveness of the human immune system.&nbsp;
Even upon testing the liquid on animal subjects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:35.760
hostile bacteria and viral agents&nbsp;
were destroyed immediately.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:42.720
Members of the O5 Council are experts at cheating&nbsp;
death, and SCP-006 is just another ace hidden up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:47.520
their sleeve in that endless battle against&nbsp;
the reaper. A secret so well-guarded that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:53.280
they’re willing to terminate even their most loyal&nbsp;
servants to keep it safe. After all, if everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.280 --> 00:14:00.160
knew about it, everyone would want it, and the&nbsp;
O5 Council are very invested in exclusivity.

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:04.320
Never normally one to rise above his station,&nbsp;
Commander McGrath couldn’t help blurt out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:07.600
“But...if it was all a lie...Private Stuart…”

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:14.000
“Is perfectly alive. All smoke and mirrors, you&nbsp;
see. And like everyone who works a 006 mission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:20.160
he won’t remember a thing. Good work, Commander&nbsp;
McGrath,” O5-2, now in perfect health, replied.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:24.720
“Now return to your post, after a visit to our&nbsp;
boys in Amnestics. There’s still plenty to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:29.280
done, and we can’t afford to dilly-dally.&nbsp;
After all, you’re not getting any younger…”

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:34.800
Now go check out “Secret Group that Runs the World&nbsp;
- SCP O5 Council Explained” and “How to Work at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:40.160
the SCP Foundation Explained” for more of the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation’s most classified inner workings!

